  "summary": "I am a software engineer with 20 years of experience. Started by building websites for myself and friends. I earned a degree in Computer Science at Harvey Mudd College. Since then I've worked on various projects, including anti-piracy software and analytics for P2P networks, data tools and consumer websites for Yellowpages.com, among other projects.\n\nI joined Riparian to help launch Helix (Government Pricing), which didn't succeed at first, but was given the opportunity to try again. Now, I lead the engineering team responsible for our revenue management platform in the Life Sciences Commercialization Department at EPG.\n\nI also serve as an elder at my local church. I am married, no kids yet.",
